---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const contactEmail = site.email || '[TODO: email@gpmm.site]';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="How GPMM uses cookies, and how you can control them."
  updated="2 November 2026"
>
  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files stored on your device that help a website function and remember
    your preferences. Some are essential; others are optional and only used with your consent.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How we use cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> — needed to run the site and remember your cookie choice. These are always active.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics cookies (optional)</strong> — help us understand how the site is used. These load only after you accept. <code>[TODO: confirm analytics tool and cookie names once added.]</code></li>
    <li><strong>Marketing cookies (optional)</strong> — such as the Meta Pixel, used for advertising. These load only after you accept. <code>[TODO: confirm if/when the Meta Pixel is used.]</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Your choice</h2>
  <p>
    When you first visit, our cookie banner lets you accept or reject optional cookies. We do
    not load analytics or marketing cookies until you accept. You can change your choice at any
    time by clearing this site's data in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies we set</h2>
  <p>
    We store your cookie choice locally in your browser (<code>gpmm-consent</code>) so we don't
    ask you again on every visit.
  </p>
  <p><code>[TODO: list specific third-party cookies, their provider, purpose and retention once analytics or the Pixel are enabled.]</code></p>

  <h2>5. More information</h2>
  <p>See our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> for how we handle personal data. Questions? Contact us at {contactEmail}.</p>
</LegalLayout>
